#### Section C — Delegation Tasks (3-Deadline System)

| Method | Route | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/api/mandate/delegation-tasks` | Create a delegation task (with or without deadline) |
| `GET` | `/api/mandate/delegation-tasks` | List all delegation tasks created by this mandate holder |
| `PATCH` | `/api/mandate/delegation-tasks/:id/extend-deadline` | Assign deadline #2 or #3 (mandate holder only) |
| `POST` | `/api/mandate/delegation-tasks/:id/mark-done` | Mark done from mandate holder side |

**`POST /api/mandate/delegation-tasks` body:**
```json
{
  "assignee_user_id": "uuid",
  "title_en": "...",
  "title_hi": "...",
  "deadline_at": "2026-08-20T18:00:00.000Z",  // null = member sets their own
  "is_important": false
}
```

**Logic for the 3-deadline lifecycle (nightly cron job + manual trigger):**
- On `PATCH /extend-deadline`: check `deadline_no < 3` → update `deadline_at`, increment `deadline_no`, update `planned_at` in `work_items`.
- If `deadline_no = 3` and deadline passes: a nightly cron `checkExpiredDelegationTasks()` runs:
  1. Finds delegation rows where `is_delegation_task=1`, `status='OPEN'`, `deadline_at < NOW()`, `deadline_no=3`
  2. Marks old row `status='MISSED'`, `auto_replaced=1`
  3. Creates a brand-new delegation row (same title, same assignee, `deadline_no=1`, no `deadline_at`) via `WorkItemService.createWorkItem()`
  4. Links `old.replaced_by = new.id`

**Member's perspective — member sets their own deadline (when `deadline_at` is null):**
Add `PATCH /api/delegations/:id/set-deadline` — only the assignee user can call this, only if `deadline_no=1` and `deadline_at IS NULL`.

